From: kind-miner
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Advise transparent huge pages for the RandomX cache

When static huge pages cannot be allocated, VirtualMemory falls back to
_mm_malloc and asks for transparent huge pages with MADV_HUGEPAGE — but only
for allocations requested with 2 MiB alignment. The dataset, the scratchpads
and the memory pool pass that alignment; the 256 MiB RandomX cache does not,
so it never gets the advice. The cache is what light mode hashes from on every
nonce, so on a machine with no reserved huge pages (the default everywhere)
light mode walks 256 MiB on 4 KiB pages.

Passing the huge page alignment gives the cache the same fallback as the rest.
Suitable for upstream.

--- a/src/crypto/rx/RxCache.cpp	2026-09-26 16:19:58.362305851 -0400
+++ b/src/crypto/rx/RxCache.cpp	2026-09-26 16:19:58.388506404 -0400
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 
 xmrig::RxCache::RxCache(bool hugePages, uint32_t nodeId)
 {
-    m_memory = new VirtualMemory(maxSize(), hugePages, false, false, nodeId);
+    m_memory = new VirtualMemory(maxSize(), hugePages, false, false, nodeId, VirtualMemory::kDefaultHugePageSize);
 
     create(m_memory->raw());
 }
